SM(399,{"n":"Deuteronomy 11","a":"Fr Stephen De Young Archives/Deuteronomy 11.mp3","d":2537.9,"s":[[0.32,"Come and study the Holy Scriptures with us as Father Stephen DeYoung teaches verse by verse on the podcast The Whole Counsel of God."],[9.04,"Father Stephen holds a PhD in Biblical Studies, and is an Orthodox priest serving at Archangel Gabriel Orthodox Church in Lafayette, Louisiana."],[21.84,"Okay, we will go ahead and get started."],[23.44,"We're going to get started in just a moment."],[25.28,"We're picking up at the beginning of Deuteronomy chapter 11."],[30.72,"So we are, as we've talked about before, in framing the book of Deuteronomy."],[36.88,"This is Moses' final address to the Israelites on the plains of Moab as they're getting ready to follow Joshua across the Jordan River into the land of Canaan to take possession of it."],[53.6,"Moses has been told that he is about to die."],[57.52,"He is preparing for that."],[59.0,"And these are his last words."],[61.56,"We finished, there's sort of two main sections to this discourse."],[68.84,"The first one was in the first few chapters where he gave sort of a historical recounting to the people of the experiences they've been through since they left Egypt."],[78.36,"And then in chapter five, we started this second part, which is most of the book, which is him going through and highlighting particular commandments, particular laws, particular teachings, uh, particular things from the books of Exodus, Leviticus, and Deuteronomy, highlighting them, preaching them, applying them to the life they're about to begin as they go into the land."],[104.04,"And he is. in sort of the midst of that"],[107.36,"And we're coming out of a section, and chapter 11 is really the end of this section."],[112.48,"It's going to refer back to some things from the last couple of chapters where God is giving these very particular commandments for what they're going to do as they enter, related to both setting up standing stones at the place where they cross the Jordan, markers where they're going to have written the commandments, and that'll be a pilgrimage site in the future."],[138.48,"And also that the Levites are being divided in two to stand on Mount Gerizim and Mount Ebal, which they're going to go in between."],[147.32,"And the Levites on Mount Gerizim are going to pronounce blessings."],[149.6,"are going to. The ones on Mount Ebal pronounce curses"],[155.4,"Not on them like dueling banjos."],[158.6,"But uh they're going to be the idea being God is communicating with them that they have this choice before them of how they're going to live once they come into the land."],[170.76,"God is going to give them the land, and then they are going to decide how they're going to live on it, what they're going to do with it, what they're going to do in it."],[177.48,"And as a result of the decisions they make, they will be blessed or they will be cursed."],[184.42,"And so as they're walking between those two things."],[188.44,"One on the right hand, one on the left hand, this is a reminder to them that they need to choose."],[194.21,"Which way they are going to go and what the destination of those those two roads is."],[201.33,"So we're in the midst of that being described to them where we left off last time."],[206.85,"So left there, elsewhere any leftover comments or uh questions, or if anybody here needs to turn off any water spigots that they left on for nearly a week, uh, we could wait for that."],[219.81,"Otherwise, we'll go ahead and pick up in uh Deuteronomy chapter 11, verse 1."],[228.21,"Therefore, you shall love the Lord your God and always keep his commandments, his ordinances, and his judgments."],[234.69,"So we'll pause right there to point out."],[236.25,"Notice how these things go together."],[238.21,"Oh gosh, he's great"],[239.61,"You shall love the Lord your God."],[241.13,"It's not just talking about having a feeling."],[244.81,"I love him."],[246.57,"But that has an actual content."],[250.09,"Loving the Lord your God means you keep his commandments."],[254.19,"You walk in the way you should walk."],[256.45,"You do what he asks you to do."],[258.77,"You don't do what he forbids you to do."],[261.91,"And we see this, this principle here comes up over and over again in the New Testament."],[266.39,"Very blatantly, Christ says, If you love me, you will keep my commandments."],[271.35,"That's pretty stark, but it means the converse is true."],[274.71,"If you do not keep his commandments, you do not love him."],[277.75,"And St. John puts it in pretty much that harsh way."],[281.29,"In 1 John."],[282.01,"He says, the person who says he loves God but hates his brother is a liar"],[287.57,"That's pretty stark."],[289.46,"If you say you love God, but you don't keep his commandment, the first of which, St."],[294.98,"John has emphasized, is love your neighbor."],[299.28,"Then you don't really love God."],[302.16,"And by saying it, you're lying."],[304.62,"So these things go together."],[307.26,"These things go together."],[308.94,"And we know they go together."],[311.18,"The only reason we think they might not go together is we've met Protestants."],[316.16,"Who tell us that you could love God and disobey Him at the same time."],[324.5,"But don't look at me."],[326.34,"I didn't think these are somehow, at least potentially."],[332.1,"Now they wouldn't say they're actually separable."],[334.18,"I want to be fair to our Protestant friends."],[336.34,"But they think hypothetically they're separable."],[339.63,"They are theoretically separable."],[342.29,"But but we know in our everyday life."],[345.75,"Like if you have a child, and you ask them to do things, or tell them not to do things, and they always disobey you, and they come and say, Oh, I love you, dad, or I love you, mom, you're not gonna believe them after a while."],[362.62,"If your spouse tells you they love you, but they cheat on you and they mistreat you, and right?"],[370.42,"And they waste all the money on frivolous things, so you don't have food to eat and you lose your."],[375.11,"No one would be like, oh, but he really loves me."],[377.19,"He said so."],[378.36,"We know that's not true."],[380.86,"We know that if you really love someone, then you are faithful to them."],[385.26,"That doesn't mean you never make a mistake."],[386.94,"When you do, what do you do?"],[388.3,"You come and repent and you apologize."],[390.32,"If you love them."],[392.8,"If you don't love them, then you might offend them and not care."],[396.5,"But if you love them, then you're gonna repent."],[399.83,"When you mess up."],[400.83,"So we know this."],[401.63,"We all understand this just from human life."],[404.37,"Well, the same is true with God."],[406.81,"Um is there supposed to be a distinction? between the charges, statutes, and judgments and commandments"],[413.45,"Like no, these are all synonyms."],[415.85,"These are all doubling down."],[417.85,"Okay, so it's just saying commandments over normal."],[420.41,"Yeah, yeah. All of these things, whether it's right, and and it's sort of deliberately not distinguishing between these things."],[430.49,"In the sense that it's like, well, all yeah, all the big things, you know, I follow."],[435.45,"You know, maybe there's some little stuff I ignore."],[438.54,"But it's, you know, whether you were so whether we're talking about because you notice the text before this doesn't differentiate between here's how you offer a sacrifice."],[447.6,"In this way."],[449.25,"Here's how you do and don't treat tre yourat your hired workers, here's how you spouse."],[457.93,"Here's how you uh deal with a what we would call a court case, how you judge a dispute."],[464.97,"God tells you how to do all of those things."],[468.02,"And you might call some of those ordinances like and some of those, you know, it's almost like they foresaw that somebody might come along in the 16th century and say, well, there's civil laws and there's moral laws, and there's doesn't matter."],[481.12,"If you love God, you're going to do every everything He tells you to do, and you're not going to do the things He tells you not to do."],[490.98,"And we've seen already here in the Torah that some of the things that we think would be minor, like offering the wrong type of incense at the wrong time, have had people dropping dead."],[503.18,"And you think, well, it's not like they killed a guy."],[505.34,"I mean, they just, you know, went in at the wrong time with the wrong incense."],[509.9,"Well, like, if God tells you to do something or not to do something, you can't be like, well, how serious are you about this, God?"],[517.92,"Like, is this like a big one?"],[520.64,"Is there some wiggle room here for me?"],[522.9,"Like, that's on it."],[524.94,"And again, the fact that someone would take that approach."],[530.27,"Like, if if on your your wedding night you you look at your wife and say, now, how faithful do I have to be?"],[539.36,"Can I like look but not touch?"],[541.62,"Like your marriage is not in a good place already."],[545.6,"Like, do you really love your wife if that's how you're thinking?"],[551.22,"So if you love God, you're not gonna be thinking, like, well, where's the wiggle room here and the stuff he told me to do?"],[557.47,"It's gonna be how can I please him?"],[562.05,"How can I honor him?"],[563.33,"How can I."],[564.15,"That's gonna be the way we think about it."],[566.87,"Would you say it's an issue of fealty and allegiance?"],[570.95,"Yeah, that's all included."],[572.39,"Yeah, all that fidelity."],[573.99,"Yeah. Faithfulness. Yeah."],[578.39,"No, today I do not speak with your children, who have not known and seen the chastening of the Lord your God, nor his greatness and mighty hand and outstretched arm, the signs and wonders he did in the midst of Egypt, to Pharaoh, king of Egypt, and all his lands, what he did to the army of Egypt, to their horse and chariots, how he made the water of the Red Sea overflow them as they pursued you, and how the Lord destroyed them to this day, what he did for you in the desert until you came to this place, and what he did to Dathan and Obiram, the sons of Eliab, the son of Reuben, how the earth opened its mouth and swallowed them up in the midst of Israel, along with their households, tents, and all the substance in their possession."],[618.67,"But your eyes saw all the great works the Lord did for you today."],[623.15,"So he's saying to them, You've been through this."],[628.12,"How are their kids going to know about it?"],[631.72,"They're going to teach, we covered that last couple of chapters."],[633.72,"They're going to be teaching their children about this."],[635.9,"How they raise their children is going to convey this to them."],[638.95,"What they've learned."],[640.47,"But this group has learned from experience."],[643.89,"Out in the wilderness."],[645.33,"They've been through this hardship."],[647.25,"They've seen some horrible things happen in terms of judgment."],[651.91,"But they've received some incredible blessings in the wilderness also from God."],[656.95,"They've seen and experienced all of this."],[659.75,"And what Moses is saying is all that that you've been through and experienced, that can be for nothing."],[666.95,"hing. If you don't learn anything from it, and you don't take anyt away from it"],[674.59,"Or it can be intensely meaningful."],[678.59,"If you learn from it and take from it and gain an understanding of God from it and the way you should live, and then you convey that to your children and your children's children."],[688.8,"And this is an important framing."],[691.74,"In terms of understanding our own lives."],[694.54,"No one who's lived a long time, and a lot of people who haven't even lived a long time, has gone through life and not gone through some stuff."],[705.22,"Has not had to deal with and experience some things."],[708.76,"And I'm not just talking about bad things, also good things, also blessings."],[712.05,"Also beautiful things."],[713.27,"But also some very hard and very difficult things."],[718.25,"We all have."],[719.93,"We tend to think in the modern world of meaning in life as if it's something objective out there."],[726.65,"Like I just need to figure out what the meaning is of all this stuff that happened to me."],[731.21,"And that's not actually how, as Moses is saying to us here, that's not actually how meaning works."],[738.09,"All of that, everything we've lived through, everything we've experienced could be completely meaningless, or it could be intensely meaningful, depending on what we do with it."],[748.33,"How we receive it, how we frame it, how it frames who we are, who we're going to become, what we're going to do in the future."],[756.61,"So the most horrible experience imaginable can become the most powerful and important experience of our life."],[767.33,"It can become a transformative experience."],[770.69,"It changes everything for us in a positive way, even though it was intensely negative."],[774.69,"That doesn't make it good."],[776.21,"It was still terrible."],[778.54,"But God can bring good out of it."],[782.14,"But that doesn't happen by automatic."],[786.46,"People can have the same experience, and one person can fall into the depths of despair, the other person can transform their life based on it."],[796.38,"Remember, we're still within this frame of talking about choosing blessings and curses."],[806.34,"This is something we have control over."],[816.58,"Not when will good things happen for us, that we don't have control over."],[820.66,"But how we'll receive both of those things, what we'll do with both of those things, how both of those things will shape us."],[828.82,"Changes that we have control over, that we have a choice to make."],[832.26,"God gives us a choice to make."],[835.46,"And things that other people might see as blessings can become curses for us based on what we choose"],[842.62,"Things that other people would see as curses can become blessings for us based on what we choose."],[848.78,"And how we choose to receive them."],[850.86,"That's what Moses is getting at here."],[853.34,"So he's talking to this group about one particular set of experiences that they all shared."],[858.6,"But this is true in general."],[861.24,"This is true more broadly."],[864.92,"Therefore, you shall keep all his commandments."],[867.4,"I command you today, that you may live and increase and go in and inherit the land you are crossing the Jordan to inherit, and may prolong your days in the land the Lord swore to give your fathers to them and their seed after them, a land flowing with milk and honey."],[884.84,"A couple of important things here."],[886.36,"A couple things he doesn't say."],[887.16,"Notice he doesn't say, keep all of these commandments, these ordinance I've given for you, and then you will have eternal life"],[894.32,"You notice he never says that?"],[897.6,"It's nowhere in the Torah."],[900.4,"Nowhere in the Torah."],[901.52,"Nowhere in the Bible does it say, if you keep the whole quote unquote law perfectly, you earn eternal life."],[909.84,"That's not a thing."],[914.16,"That's not a promise God ever makes."],[916.72,"What does he say?"],[919.92,"He says, if you keep the commandments and ordinances, if you live the way I'm describing to you to live, you will have a long and flourishing life in the land."],[931.38,"And this gets to the purpose of the commandments"],[933.58,"If you don't, you won't."],[938.78,"He doesn't give these commandments as a set of hoops you need to jump through to get to heaven."],[945.84,"Or eternal life or whatever."],[947.76,"These aren't a bunch of hoops."],[949.12,"This isn't a test."],[953.6,"This certainly isn't God putting a fast one on Israel for several centuries by giving them a bunch of rules they're unable to follow and then attacking them for not following them."],[965.76,"Which is absurd."],[966.32,"absurd. That's Sorry, Martin Luther."],[971.78,"The idea that God would give commandments, tell them they need to keep them, and, and they can't he knows they can't."],[979.26,"For centuries. That's an obscene suggestion about the character of God."],[986.86,"No, it's if you want to live a flourishing and successful human life, then the God who created humanity, who created us as humans."],[996.23,"And knows how we ought to live in the world, tells us here's how to live in the world."],[1004.84,"That's what it is."],[1006.44,"He makes rules."],[1008.6,"If we want to call them rules, just call them rules."],[1011.16,"He makes rules for the same reason a parent makes rules."],[1015.88,"Because he loves his children."],[1019.76,"He wants to see them come to maturity."],[1023.06,"To flourish in life."],[1025.22,"Be successful. To have love, to have joy in their life."],[1027.86,"That's what he wants for them."],[1029.14,"And he makes these rules for that reason."],[1034.23,"If a parent made rules for their children just arbitrarily, just to test them."],[1039.59,"Like they're doing a prolonged experiment in child development or something."],[1042.79,"We'd say that's not a good parent."],[1048.52,"That's what that's how God is."],[1050.2,"A parent makes rules."],[1051.34,"I couldn't go play in the street when I was a kid because my parents didn't want me to get hit by a car."],[1057.42,"When I was a stupid kid, I may have said, Oh, don't we have fun?"],[1062.27,"Because I was a stupid kid."],[1064.83,"Thought that about most of the rules my parents made."],[1067.61,"And my parents weren't perfect."],[1071.79,"Some of their rules were probably for other reasons, selfish reasons, paranoid reasons, you know, whatever."],[1076.83,"Because they're human and sinful and not perfect."],[1079.84,"But their intent."],[1082.18,"Their intent was to help me grow up and come to maturity and flourish."],[1087.59,"And God, unlike our human parents, isn't sinful and doesn't make those kind of mistakes."],[1093.51,"But so that's what he's laying out."],[1096.19,"Okay? He says, I'm I'm giving this to you, as we've already seen."],[1100.71,"He's giving them the land."],[1102.07,"He didn't say, okay, here's the Torah and all the commandments"],[1106.51,"Once you have kept them perfectly for 40 years, I will give you the land."],[1111.65,"Or for some other period of time."],[1113.81,"In fact, we've already seen earlier, just a couple chapters ago, Moses was saying that quite deliberately."],[1119.43,"When you go into the land, don't start thinking it's because there's something good about you."],[1123.36,"You didn't keep the, you didn't even have the commandments, let alone keep them in Egypt."],[1127.36,"And once you got them in the desert, you started breaking them from day one."],[1130.4,"Remember the golden calf?"],[1131.6,"Remember the right?"],[1132.96,"Like you haven't kept them for five seconds."],[1135.62,"God's giving you the land."],[1137.38,"Gratis. Here it is."],[1141.11,"Pure gift of his grace."],[1142.71,"But if you want to receive, it if you want to live there and prosper there and keep it."],[1149.57,"And not get driven out."],[1151.35,"The way the people you're driving out are getting driven out, then you need to live in a certain way."],[1158.56,"You need to be faithful."],[1160.16,"As we've been talking about."],[1161.84,"This is fundamentally the same thing St."],[1163.84,"Paul says in the New Testament."],[1166.0,"Christ died for us before we existed, everyone in this room."],[1170.8,"By millennia. Okay."],[1175.36,"He did that for us."],[1177.94,"For our salvation."],[1179.06,"So he's just given to us."],[1180.14,"Eternal life. He gives us eternal life free."],[1182.92,"But if we want to take possession of it, we need to live in a certain way, faithfully."],[1186.04,"It's the same thing"],[1189.94,"To God our Savior."],[1193.78,"So the gospel in the Torah is the same as the gospel in the New Testament."],[1199.86,"It's just we now have the fullness of it."],[1202.5,"We're not just talking about a strip of land."],[1206.5,"That strip of land was an image."],[1209.14,"It was an icon."],[1210.34,"It was a picture."],[1212.52,"Of the real salvation that was to come in Christ."],[1215.48,"Because as long as their life might be in the land that the Lord their God was giving them, it had an end."],[1220.6,"They still died."],[1224.04,"Meaning, problem from Genesis 3 not really solved yet."],[1228.84,"Because Canaan wasn't Eden"],[1235.28,"It wasn't paradise."],[1237.76,"And even though it wasn't, they even got kicked out again by the time we're at the end of the Old Testament."],[1242.64,"Even from that."],[1244.96,"But it was a picture of what was coming in Christ."],[1248.96,"And so the contours of that image, for it to be an image, the contours are the same."],[1256.24,"For the land you go to inherit is not like the land of Egypt from which you came, where you sowed your seed and watered it by foot as a vegetable garden."],[1265.28,"But the land you are crossing over to inherit is a land of hills and plains, which drinks water from the rain of heaven."],[1272.08,"A land the Lord your God looks upon, the eyes of the Lord your God are always on it from the beginning of the year to the very end of the year."],[1280.44,"So he's using this as an image."],[1283.01,"So what's he talking about with walking around on foot with the garden?"],[1286.21,"The idea here is in Egypt the crops grow based on the swelling of the Nile in the spring."],[1295.99,"The Nile swells, it washes down silt and deposits it on the banks."],[1301.75,"Then the water level goes down, they plant in that silt."],[1305.27,"They've got to irrigate, bring water from the Nile up into the."],[1309.25,"That's how it works."],[1311.09,"They're going now into Canaan."],[1313.91,"Where water is less scarce."],[1316.29,"They're not getting water out of a river, but the rains come in off the Mediterranean, and you get snow up on a few of the mountaintops."],[1325.45,"And that water runs down."],[1327.66,"And the rains bring water."],[1330.35,"And so God is saying the land you're going into."],[1334.69,"The land he's bringing them to sort of reflects the character of what he's talking about."],[1341.27,"In Egypt, you're bringing forth crops by the sweat of your brow."],[1345.69,"Working the fields in a different way."],[1347.45,"It's sort of an image of, remember the curse on Adam in Genesis 3."],[1351.46,"That that's how he was going to have to bring forth food."],[1354.52,"Whereas Canaan is, again, not quite eaten, but a little more edenic in the sense that remember Eden was watered by those rivers that came out from the center."],[1364.94,"It's watered by God."],[1366.16,"This land also, in the sense of the rain, is watered by God."],[1372.05,"So the land he's bringing them into is a land of a lot more abundance than Egypt."],[1378.86,"It is not going to be as hard as Egypt."],[1380.78,"He's bringing them to a better land than Egypt."],[1385.2,"But the reason it's better is that there's still going to have to be this constant interdependence between them and God."],[1393.04,"So if you earnestly obey all his commandments, I command you today to love the Lord your God and serve him with all your heart and with all your soul, then he will give you rain for your land in its season, the early rain and the latter rain, that you may gather in your grain wine and olive oil."],[1411.08,"I will also send grass in your fields for your cattle, that you may eat and be filled."],[1416.2,"Take heed to yourselves, lest your heart be deceived, and you transgress and serve other gods and worship them, lest the Lord's anger be aroused against you and ye shut up heaven, so there may be no rain, and the land yield no produce, and you perish quickly from the good land the Lord gave you."],[1434.68,"Okay, so what's this part about?"],[1436.44,"Well, it's building off of what we were just saying."],[1438.64,"Okay, so the examples God gives here are examples that are beyond their control."],[1444.68,"Meaning they can't control. the rains, coming in their seasons"],[1452.72,"One year you get more rain, one rain you get less rain."],[1457.92,"We understand they don't have a way to control that."],[1461.89,"The grass for their livestock to feed on."],[1465.17,"You don't go and plant, at least in those days, you didn't go and plant grass."],[1472.37,"The herds grazed out there in the fields."],[1474.85,"That stuff just grew because of the rain."],[1477.42,"You didn't go out and plant it and water it or tend it."],[1480.88,"Plow it. Okay, so these are things that are going to come or not come, and that's God's pointing out, that's based on God's providence."],[1490.3,"And what he does."],[1492.96,"Why does he bring up other gods here?"],[1496.24,"Well, the main one running around Canaan is Baal, who's a storm god."],[1500.96,"Okay. And why do they keep worshiping Baal?"],[1507.12,"Have you ever thought about?"],[1508.4,"Why do they keep doing that?"],[1509.78,"But not just that he's supposed to, because God says he's gonna send rain."],[1515.34,"So why Baal?"],[1517.64,"Well, because Yahweh, the God of Israel, God here, capital G God, who's gonna send the rain."],[1524.14,"He' alsready told us he doesn't take bribes in the last chapter."],[1528.18,"You can't influence him."],[1530.18,"You can't get him to do what you want."],[1533.04,"What does he say here in terms of him sending the rain?"],[1537.44,"You're faithful, you love me, you live as I tell you to, I will send the rain, and I will I will cause the grass to grow."],[1545.3,"Well that that's complicated."],[1547.34,"That's complicated and tricky."],[1549.74,"So I can go with that."],[1551.76,"Try and live my whole life pleasing to God of Israel."],[1555.92,"Or I can sacrifice a couple of goats to Baal, maybe sleep with a shrine prostitute or two during a feast."],[1566.72,"And Baal says he guarantees he's gonna send me right"],[1570.8,"That whole feast thing's kind of fun."],[1573.2,"That's why It's not that they actually liked Baal or thought there was something great about Bale."],[1582.49,"It was the illusion of putting things in their own control."],[1589.37,"The illusion that no, I'm the one in charge here."],[1593.69,"And because I'm the one in charge here, I don't have to worry about how God wants me to live."],[1602.17,"I can just take control of these levers."],[1606.59,"For my own for my own prosperity."],[1609.73,"And so I wager, most of you, unless any of you have secretly been to Bohemian Grove or something, have never been tempted to worship Baal."],[1618.73,"Like literally. But this is still very much a temptation for us."],[1625.0,"This is one of the things that besets humanity all the time."],[1627.8,"We want to take control of the levers of power, the levers that make the world work."],[1633.34,"Whether it's money, fame."],[1636.11,"What we do for a living, we want to get a hold of those, just control of our own life, even at a very small level."],[1643.92,"Because if we feel like we're in control, that means we don't have to worry about God."],[1651.52,"Or anybody else, for that matter."],[1655.04,"I'm the captain of my own destiny."],[1660.69,"What's interesting is God doesn't say, no, it's out of your control."],[1667.09,"I manipulate you like a puppet master."],[1669.01,"Sorry, Calvinists. That's not what God says."],[1672.71,"God's been telling them that they're in control."],[1677.19,"God's been telling them you're in control by how you choose to live."],[1683.43,"You're in control by how you choose to react and give meaning to the things that happen in your life."],[1689.99,"He doesn't say you have no control."],[1693.75,"He says you are in control."],[1697.25,"But it's not easy."],[1697.65,"'s not easy It."],[1700.77,"It's not something you could bribe your way out of"],[1707.37,"It's not something you can shortcut."],[1711.77,"It's something that requires your whole life and your attention and your devotion and your work."],[1720.3,"To live faithfully to your God."],[1724.14,"And then you will see how you flourish and how these things work out."],[1728.78,"There's no shortcutting it."],[1730.54,"No amount of money will shortcut it."],[1733.18,"No amount of bribes to spiritual powers will shortcut it."],[1738.39,"No amount of our insistence."],[1740.0,"That no, really I'm I'm the one in charge, actually works."],[1746.04,"And so that's the that's always the temptation."],[1749.88,"The shortcut. Because remember, that that was the temptation with the serpent in Genesis 3."],[1760.44,"Adam and Eve were created to become like God."],[1765.88,"That was the purpose of their creation."],[1768.04,"That they would one day become like God."],[1771.0,"And the fathers even say there would have come a day when they could have eaten of the tree of the knowledge of good and evil when they were prepared for it."],[1777.0,"The tree itself was not evil."],[1780.2,"But what does the serpent covenant do?"],[1782.76,"Here's a shortcut."],[1784.44,"Eat it now, and you'll become like God right now."],[1789.16,"Just flip to the back of the book, see how it ends"],[1797.36,"That's the very first temptation."],[1800.02,"And what God is pointing to here for the ancient Israelites."],[1803.08,"Is here's another version that temptation's going to take for you."],[1807.24,"Go worship Baal."],[1808.68,"Go worship Moloch."],[1809.88,"Go worship these other gods that try and shortcut this whole thing."],[1814.9,"It's a lot easier than going out there at work in the fields and praying and living faithfully to God and all that, and trusting in Him to bring the rain in its season."],[1824.34,"And again, we face versions of that temptation all the time"],[1829.11,"Quick, easy shortcut way."],[1831.03,"To get the things we think we want"],[1834.8,"Therefore, you shall lay up these words of mine in your heart and in your soul and bind them as a sign on your hand."],[1841.44,"They shall be immovable before your eyes."],[1847.52,"Now, you may be familiar with sort of the literal way that later Judaism takes this with phylacteries."],[1853.7,"With the little scrolls that they have on their foreheads and bound onto their hands and were in their heart."],[1860.98,"What you may not know is that Christians for many centuries had phylacteries with like Bible verses, from the New Testament and things that they'd wear."],[1873.94,"And those kind of things."],[1874.82,"So that's not purely a Jewish practice, but of course, the core of this is not that literal sense."],[1883.95,"There may be something good about that literal sense, but only if that literal sense is combined with the broader sense."],[1892.44,"Having something physically over your heart and your chest is less important than actually having it in your heart."],[1901.82,"Actually having it in your mind, as opposed to just having it stuck to your forehead."],[1906.8,"Like, but those physical things serve as reminders."],[1909.94,"Because you feel them, you see them."],[1911.78,"They serve as reminders."],[1913.88,"That help you get them into your heart or into your head."],[1916.44,"That's why those practices, came came into being."],[1920.51,"But the idea here is that these are the things you're seeing and hearing and thinking about all the time."],[1927.47,"And this is one of the issues."],[1931.6,"Beyond this is a practical pastoral issue, beyond all the theological issues with iconoclasm."],[1938.77,"This is one of the very practical and pastoral problems with iconoclasm."],[1944.39,"Is once you remove the idea of holy images from the picture."],[1951.47,"Once you remove uh all of that, and you're down to whitewashed walls, even in your church."],[1958.85,"When you're worried, like some of my seminary professors were in Protestant seminary, that if you even put a cross at the front of your church, someone might make it an idol."],[1968.13,"Then what are people looking at and being reminded of all the time during the day?"],[1975.89,"There's plenty of other things in the world, especially our world, to look at."],[1980.61,"On your computer, on your television screen, on your phone, hanging on walls, on billboards, on the sides of buildings, everywhere all the time."],[1991.25,"And if we preclude holy images, what are we left with?"],[1996.69,"We're left with profane images."],[1999.01,"We're left with profane images at best."],[2003.5,"If not outright, you know, sinfulness and wickedness."],[2007.23,"And so, yeah, that's the the."],[2011.79,"I'm not talking about Christianity here."],[2014.35,"Judy, ancient Israelite worship and Jewish worship and Jewish life was never iconoclastic."],[2026.19,"Right before the Christian period."],[2027.79,"You have the synagogues who've got imagery all over them."],[2030.61,"People's homes, including these phylacteries."],[2033.42,"These are physical things that you see that remind you."],[2037.04,"They carry your mind back to holy things, back to good things."],[2043.53,"And that's what Moses is talking about here."],[2045.21,"These are the things that should be rolling around in our heads"],[2045.49,"These are the things we should be obsessing about."],[2052.43,"Not the pop song that got stuck in my head."],[2054.51,"Not the commercial jingle that got stuck in my head."],[2057.07,"How about a traparian?"],[2058.43,"It wouldn't hurt anything."],[2060.0,"Like a hymn."],[2061.12,"That wouldn't hurt anything if that was rattling around instead."],[2063.68,"In fact, it'd be a lot better."],[2065.84,"Because all those things getting stuck in our head are shaping us in different ways."],[2069.6,"You shall teach them to your children, speaking of them when you sit in your house and walk by the way."],[2075.48,"When you lie down and rise up, you shall also write them on the doorposts of your house and your gates, that your days and the days of your sons may be multiplied in the land the Lord swore to give your fathers like days of heaven on earth."],[2089.88,"So, yeah, here we have the same thing your doorposts, your house, the walls."],[2096.21,"This is what you talk about with your kids."],[2098.37,"This is the subject of conversation around the dinner table."],[2102.45,"Ha ha, dinner table."],[2103.81,"Yeah, I know."],[2104.69,"Um, but right, this is these are the things that are the focus."],[2109.73,"And again, notice you know, we think about these things very individualistically, but that's not the language they're talked about in."],[2118.05,"This is what your family life, this is what your community life is focused on."],[2124.91,"This isn't your personal religious beliefs, that you go off and do by yourself."],[2129.47,"And we don't talk about in public."],[2131.23,"This is what the the communal life is focused on."],[2139.11,"For if you carefully keep all these commandments, I command you today to love the Lord your God, to walk in all his ways, and to hold fast to him."],[2148.39,"Those three things, that's a summary of all the commandments."],[2153.51,"Love the Lord your God, walk in all his ways, hold fast to him."],[2159.91,"That last one is about loyalty and allegiance."],[2162.09,"Holding fast to him."],[2164.89,"That's it. That covers everything."],[2167.45,"Then the Lord will cast out all these nations from before your face, and you will inherit greater and mightier nations than yourselves."],[2175.29,"Every place the sole of your foot treads shall be yours from the desert and anti Lebanon, which is not against Lebanon, it's instead of Lebanon."],[2189.81,"And from the great Euphrates River, even to the western sea, shall be your territory."],[2194.29,"No man shall be able to stand against your face."],[2196.69,"The Lord your God will put the dread and the fear of you upon all the land where you tread, in the manner the Lord said to you."],[2204.69,"So he's saying, Not only will you go in and take possession of this land I'm giving you, you're not even really gonna have to fight."],[2213.65,"All these people, even though they're more powerful than you, he's like, Yeah, I know they're bigger than you, stronger than you."],[2218.13,"They have actual militaries, and you don't, they have walled cities, they weigh outber.num you, they're way more powerful than you, but you're not even gonna have to fight because they're gonna be scared of you"],[2228.81,"Why are they gonna be scared of Israel?"],[2230.81,"Because of Israel's God."],[2233.37,"That's why they're gonna be scared."],[2235.38,"And so you will you will walk right into this as long as you remain faithful."],[2240.5,"You don't have to be afraid of anything as long as you remain faithful."],[2246.55,"That's what he's saying."],[2248.07,"And now we get a summary."],[2251.11,"Behold, I set before you today a blessing and a curse."],[2254.79,"The blessing if you obey the commandments of the Lord your God, I command you today, and the curse if you do not obey the commandments of the Lord your God."],[2262.31,"But go astray from the way I command you today, and go after different gods you have not known."],[2268.83,"Now notice that phrase that gods you have not known."],[2274.03,"That doesn't mean like, oh, you've never heard the name Baal before."],[2277.71,"Obviously they have."],[2278.51,"Remember Baal Peor in numbers."],[2281.31,"That's not what they're talking about."],[2282.99,"Sorry, they haven't known."],[2284.99,"Meaning God knows the people of Israel, and they know God."],[2290.59,"They've come to know God between Egypt and today."],[2296.75,"God has revealed Himself to them."],[2298.59,"They know who He is."],[2300.59,"He knows who they are."],[2302.27,"They have this relationship."],[2306.16,"These other gods are strangers."],[2308.64,"They haven't done anything for Israel."],[2309.84,"Israel Where were they when was in the desert?"],[2310.08,"When they were slaves in Egypt"],[2316.36,"When they're these are strangers."],[2318.04,"These are outsiders."],[2321.64,"That's what he means by these are gods you haven't known."],[2324.2,"They're nothing to you."],[2327.8,"Whereas God is the one who has done all of this for them."],[2331.08,"God is the one who has revealed himself to them."],[2334.36,"The word that's used in the Hebrew for know here is the same word that's used in uh Genesis chapter 4, where it says, Adam knew his wife, and she brought forth a son."],[2350.44,"That's not a euphemism."],[2351.56,"That's a literal, it's the verb to know."],[2353.64,"It's yada, um, in Hebrew."],[2356.56,"So that's the same."],[2358.74,"So obviously it's not literal, but God is comparing the intimacy of his relationship to Israel, to the relationship between a husband and wife."],[2368.9,"That kind of intimacy."],[2371.14,"Now it shall be when the Lord your God brings you into this land you are to inherit, you shall put the blessing on Mount Gerizim and the curse on Mount Ebal."],[2379.86,"That's what we were talking about before."],[2381.06,"The the Levites who are doing the blessing are on Mount Gerizim."],[2384.1,"Levites who are doing the cursing are on Mount Ebal when they're coming in."],[2388.1,"Indeed, are they not on the other side of the Jordan toward the setting sun in the land of Canaan, the area that lies to the west near Gilgal, beside the lofty oak?"],[2398.82,"oak. There's an"],[2408.78,"Yes, they're on the mountains pronouncing blessings, God's blessings on the one mountain and God's curses on the other mountain."],[2416.46,"And the Israelites are walking into the land between the two."],[2420.38,"The idea being that they have to choose which way they're gonna go."],[2426.2,"So it's an enactment of that."],[2429.16,"Anyway, is it like doorposts?"],[2431.32,"In the symbol."],[2432.28,"Or was it more like a fork in the road?"],[2434.68,"It's more like a fork in the road."],[2436.6,"Yeah. Because they're going between the mountains, in this valley."],[2439.77,"That you could go to the left or to the right."],[2441.49,"Yeah. And is this the whole reason why, like the set um? the Samaritans were superfixing on Mount Garrison"],[2447.53,"It's part of it."],[2448.41,"Okay. Yes. Rare instance you're tracking."],[2452.81,"Tracking well. So we'll get into that."],[2455.93,"Yeah, here in a few minutes when we get into the next chapter."],[2458.89,"Yeah, because remember the chapter divisions weren't there originally."],[2463.13,"For you will cross over the Jordan and go in to inherit the land the Lord your God has given you, and you will inherit it all your days and dwell in it."],[2470.09,"Therefore you shall be careful to do all the ordinances and judgments I set before you today."],[2474.97,"So as they're coming in, they're receiving it, but they're being called upon to make this choice."],[2482.03,"About how they're gonna live in the land."],[2484.97,"And and what the consequence of that. is uh is going to be"],[2491.25,"Okay, so here we have a chapter break, and that's a good chapter break in terms of the content, but we have to remember that's not originally there, because we're going to talk about the Samaritans in a minute."],[2501.25,"Because there's a shift in topics, and the Samaritans, and in their edit of the Samaritan Pentateuch, they're going to draw a couple things together that aren't necessarily drawn together in the text."],[2515.41,"Listen next time as Father Stephen DeYoung continues his study of the scriptures on the Whole Counsel of God."],[2522.77,"Father Stephen's email address is wholecounsel at ancientfaith.com."],[2528.13,"That's wholecounsel at ancientfaith.com."]],"o":[{"t":21.84,"lv":2,"h":"Where we are: Moses' final address","b":"<ul><li class=\"d0\">Picking up at start of <b>Deuteronomy 11</b>; framing the book</li><li class=\"d0\"><b>Moses' final address</b> on plains of <b>Moab</b></li><li class=\"d1\">about to follow <b>Joshua</b> across Jordan into Canaan</li><li class=\"d1\">told he is <b>about to die</b> - \"these are his last words\"</li><li class=\"d0\">Two main sections of discourse</li><li class=\"d1\">first: <b>historical recounting</b> since Egypt (first chapters)</li><li class=\"d1\">second (from ch. 5, most of book): <b>highlighting commandments</b> from Exodus, Leviticus, Deuteronomy - preaching, applying to life in the land</li><li class=\"d0\">Ch. 11 = <b>end of this section</b></li><li class=\"d1\">refers back to last chapters: <b>standing stones</b> at the Jordan crossing - commandments written, future <b>pilgrimage site</b></li><li class=\"d1\">Levites split to <b>Mt Gerizim</b> (blessings) and <b>Mt Ebal</b> (curses) - \"not like dueling banjos\"</li><li class=\"d0\">The point: a <b>choice</b> before them</li><li class=\"d1\">God gives land → <b>they decide</b> how to live in it</li><li class=\"d1\">walking between the two mountains = <b>right hand / left hand</b>, which road and where it ends</li></ul>"},{"t":219.81,"lv":2,"h":"Deut 11:1 - Love means keeping commandments","b":"<ul><li class=\"d0\"><b>11:1</b> \"Love the Lord your God and always keep his commandments, ordinances, judgments\"</li><li class=\"d0\">Love has <b>actual content</b>, not just a feeling</li><li class=\"d1\">loving God = <b>keep commandments</b>, walk the way, do what he asks, not what he forbids</li><li class=\"d1\">Christ: \"<b>If you love me, you will keep my commandments</b>\"</li><li class=\"d1\">converse true: don't keep them → <b>don't love him</b></li><li class=\"d1\"><b>1 John</b>: says he loves God but hates his brother = <b>a liar</b>; first commandment John stresses = love your neighbor</li><li class=\"d0\">Only reason we think they separate: \"we've met <b>Protestants</b>\"</li><li class=\"d1\">fair: they wouldn't say separable in practice - <b>theoretically</b> separable</li><li class=\"d0\">Human analogies</li><li class=\"d1\">child who always disobeys but says \"I love you\" - <b>you stop believing</b></li><li class=\"d1\">spouse who cheats, mistreats, wastes the money, \"but he said so\" - <b>not true</b></li><li class=\"d1\">loving someone = <b>faithful</b>; mistakes → you <b>repent and apologize</b>; if you don't love, you offend and don't care</li></ul>"},{"t":406.81,"lv":3,"h":"Q: charges, statutes, judgments - any distinction?","b":"<ul><li class=\"d0\">Q: distinction between <b>charges, statutes, judgments, commandments</b>?</li><li class=\"d1\">No - <b>synonyms</b>, \"doubling down\"; deliberately <b>not distinguishing</b></li><li class=\"d0\">Text before doesn't separate: how to offer <b>sacrifice</b>, treat <b>hired workers</b>, <b>spouse</b>, judge a <b>court dispute</b></li><li class=\"d1\">some \"ordinances\", some other - \"as if they foresaw\" the <b>16th century</b> split into <b>civil vs. moral laws</b></li><li class=\"d1\">doesn't matter: if you love God, you do <b>everything</b> he says</li><li class=\"d0\">Torah already shows \"minor\" things aren't: <b>wrong incense at wrong time</b> → people dropping dead</li><li class=\"d1\">can't ask God \"how serious are you about this? <b>wiggle room</b>?\"</li><li class=\"d0\">Wedding-night analogy: \"how faithful do I have to be? <b>look but not touch</b>?\" → marriage already in a bad place</li><li class=\"d1\">if you love God: \"how can I <b>please</b> him, <b>honor</b> him?\"</li><li class=\"d1\">comment: <b>fealty and allegiance</b>, fidelity, faithfulness - \"all included\"</li></ul>"},{"t":578.39,"lv":2,"h":"11:2-7 - You saw it; will it mean anything?","b":"<ul><li class=\"d0\"><b>11:2-7</b> \"I do not speak with your children, who have not known the <b>chastening of the Lord</b>...\"</li><li class=\"d1\">recounts <b>Egypt</b>, Pharaoh, <b>Red Sea</b>, wilderness, <b>Dathan and Abiram</b> swallowed by earth</li><li class=\"d1\">\"your eyes saw all the great works\"</li><li class=\"d0\">Children will learn via <b>teaching</b> (last chapters) - but <b>this generation learned from experience</b></li><li class=\"d1\">hardship, horrible <b>judgments</b>, but also <b>incredible blessings</b></li><li class=\"d0\">All of it \"can be <b>for nothing</b>\" if you take nothing away</li><li class=\"d1\">or <b>intensely meaningful</b> if you learn, understand God, live it, <b>convey to children and grandchildren</b></li></ul>"},{"t":688.8,"lv":3,"h":"How meaning works in our own lives","b":"<ul><li class=\"d0\">Important framing for <b>our own lives</b></li><li class=\"d1\">everyone who has lived has \"gone through some stuff\" - <b>good and hard</b></li><li class=\"d0\">Modern idea: meaning is <b>objective, out there</b>, \"I just need to figure out the meaning of what happened\"</li><li class=\"d1\"><b>not how meaning works</b> (Moses' point)</li><li class=\"d1\">experience <b>meaningless or intensely meaningful</b> depending on <b>what we do with it</b></li><li class=\"d0\">Most horrible experience → can become <b>most powerful, transformative</b> one</li><li class=\"d1\">doesn't make it good - \"still terrible\" - but <b>God can bring good out of it</b></li><li class=\"d1\"><b>not automatic</b>: same experience, one falls into <b>despair</b>, another is <b>transformed</b></li><li class=\"d0\">Still in frame of <b>blessings and curses</b>: what we control</li><li class=\"d1\">not <b>when good things happen</b> - but <b>how we receive</b> them and what they do to us</li><li class=\"d1\">things others see as blessings → <b>curses for us</b>; and reverse</li></ul>"},{"t":864.92,"lv":2,"h":"11:8-9 - Keep the commandments, live long in the land","b":"<ul><li class=\"d0\"><b>11:8-9</b> keep all commandments → <b>live, increase, inherit</b>, prolong days in land flowing with <b>milk and honey</b></li><li class=\"d0\">What he <b>doesn't say</b>: keep the law → <b>eternal life</b></li><li class=\"d1\">nowhere in Torah, <b>nowhere in the Bible</b>: keep \"the law\" perfectly, earn eternal life</li><li class=\"d1\">promise is <b>long, flourishing life in the land</b> - if not, you won't</li><li class=\"d0\">Purpose of commandments</li><li class=\"d1\"><b>not hoops</b> to get to heaven, not a test</li><li class=\"d1\">not God \"putting a fast one on Israel\" - rules they can't follow, then attacking them → \"absurd. Sorry, <b>Martin Luther</b>\"</li><li class=\"d1\">God giving commandments he <b>knows they can't keep</b>, for centuries = \"<b>obscene</b> suggestion about the character of God\"</li><li class=\"d0\">Real reason: Creator knows <b>how humans flourish</b> - \"here's how to live\"</li><li class=\"d1\">rules for same reason a <b>parent</b> makes them: <b>loves his children</b>, wants maturity, success, love, joy</li><li class=\"d1\">arbitrary rules to test = \"not a good parent\"</li></ul>"},{"t":1050.2,"lv":3,"h":"Parent analogy; land is a gift","b":"<ul><li class=\"d0\">His own parents: \"couldn't play in the <b>street</b>\" - <b>car</b></li><li class=\"d1\">human parents' rules sometimes selfish, paranoid - <b>God isn't sinful</b>, no such mistakes</li><li class=\"d0\">Land is <b>gratis</b>, not earned</li><li class=\"d1\">didn't say \"keep Torah perfectly 40 years, then land\"</li><li class=\"d1\">ch. 9: don't think it's because <b>you're good</b> - no commandments in Egypt, broke them <b>from day one</b> (<b>golden calf</b>)</li><li class=\"d1\">\"pure gift of his <b>grace</b>\"</li><li class=\"d0\">To <b>receive/keep</b> it and not be <b>driven out</b> like the Canaanites → live <b>faithfully</b></li><li class=\"d1\">same as <b>St. Paul</b>: Christ died for us <b>millennia</b> before we existed - eternal life <b>free</b>; to take possession, live faithfully</li><li class=\"d1\"><b>gospel in the Torah = gospel in New Testament</b>, now the <b>fullness</b></li></ul>"},{"t":1202.5,"lv":3,"h":"The land as icon","b":"<ul><li class=\"d0\">Strip of land = <b>image, icon, picture</b> of salvation in Christ</li><li class=\"d1\">life in land had <b>an end</b> - \"they still died\" → <b>Genesis 3 problem</b> not solved</li><li class=\"d1\">\"<b>Canaan wasn't Eden</b>\", wasn't paradise - <b>kicked out again</b> by end of OT</li><li class=\"d0\">But contours of the image are the same</li></ul>"},{"t":1256.24,"lv":2,"h":"11:10-12 - Egypt vs. Canaan: watered by foot or by heaven","b":"<ul><li class=\"d0\"><b>11:10-12</b> Egypt: sow seed, \"<b>water it by foot</b> as a vegetable garden\"; Canaan: hills and plains, <b>rain of heaven</b>, <b>eyes of the Lord always on it</b></li><li class=\"d0\">Egypt's farming</li><li class=\"d1\">crops depend on <b>Nile swelling</b> in spring → <b>silt</b> on banks</li><li class=\"d1\">water drops, plant in silt, <b>irrigate</b> from the Nile</li><li class=\"d0\">Canaan</li><li class=\"d1\"><b>rains</b> off the Mediterranean, <b>snow</b> on a few mountaintops, runoff</li><li class=\"d0\">Image of <b>Genesis 3</b></li><li class=\"d1\">Egypt = bring forth crops by <b>sweat of the brow</b> (curse on Adam)</li><li class=\"d1\">Canaan = \"a little more <b>edenic</b>\" - Eden watered by rivers from the center; Canaan <b>watered by God</b></li><li class=\"d0\"><b>Better, more abundant</b> land - but <b>constant interdependence</b> between them and God</li></ul>"},{"t":1393.04,"lv":2,"h":"11:13-17 - Rain, grass, and other gods","b":"<ul><li class=\"d0\"><b>11:13-17</b> obey, love and serve with <b>all heart and soul</b> → <b>early and latter rain</b>, grain, wine, oil, <b>grass for cattle</b></li><li class=\"d0\">Warning: heart <b>deceived</b> → serve other gods → <b>heaven shut</b>, no rain, perish from the good land</li><li class=\"d0\">Examples are things <b>beyond their control</b></li><li class=\"d1\">rains in season - more one year, less another</li><li class=\"d1\"><b>grass</b> for herds - not planted or watered then, just grew from the rain → <b>God's providence</b></li><li class=\"d0\">Why <b>other gods</b>? Main one in Canaan: <b>Baal</b>, a <b>storm god</b></li><li class=\"d1\">why do they keep worshiping him? <b>Yahweh</b> \"doesn't take bribes\" (last chapter) - can't be influenced</li><li class=\"d1\">God: be faithful, love me, live as I say → I send rain - \"complicated and tricky\"</li><li class=\"d1\">alternative: sacrifice a couple goats to Baal, \"<b>shrine prostitute</b> or two during a feast\" - <b>guaranteed rain</b>, and \"that feast thing's kind of fun\"</li></ul>"},{"t":1573.2,"lv":3,"h":"The illusion of control","b":"<ul><li class=\"d0\">Not that they liked Baal - the <b>illusion of putting things in their own control</b></li><li class=\"d1\">\"I'm the one in charge\" → <b>don't have to worry</b> how God wants me to live; just take the <b>levers</b></li><li class=\"d0\">Most here never tempted to worship Baal (\"unless... <b>Bohemian Grove</b>\") - but <b>still our temptation</b></li><li class=\"d1\">levers: <b>money, fame, work</b> - \"<b>captain of my own destiny</b>\"</li><li class=\"d0\">God doesn't say it's out of your control - \"<b>puppet master</b>, sorry <b>Calvinists</b>\"</li><li class=\"d1\">says <b>you are in control</b>: how you <b>live</b>, how you <b>react and give meaning</b></li><li class=\"d1\">but <b>not easy</b>: no bribing out, <b>no shortcut</b>; takes <b>whole life, attention, devotion, work</b></li><li class=\"d1\">no amount of <b>money</b>, no <b>bribes to spiritual powers</b>, no insisting \"I'm in charge\" works</li></ul>"},{"t":1746.04,"lv":3,"h":"The shortcut: serpent in Genesis 3","b":"<ul><li class=\"d0\">Always the temptation: <b>the shortcut</b></li><li class=\"d1\"><b>serpent</b> in Gen 3: Adam and Eve created to <b>become like God</b> - that was the purpose</li><li class=\"d1\">fathers: a day would have come to eat of the <b>tree</b> when <b>prepared</b> - tree not evil</li><li class=\"d1\">serpent: \"eat it <b>now</b>, become like God <b>right now</b>\" - \"flip to the back of the book, see how it ends\"</li><li class=\"d0\">Israel's version: <b>Baal, Moloch</b>, other gods</li><li class=\"d1\">easier than working fields, <b>praying</b>, living faithfully, <b>trusting him</b> for rain</li><li class=\"d1\">\"we face versions of that all the time\" - quick, easy way to get what we think we want</li></ul>"},{"t":1834.8,"lv":2,"h":"11:18-21 - Words in heart, hand, doorposts","b":"<ul><li class=\"d0\"><b>11:18-21</b> lay up my words in <b>heart and soul</b>, bind as <b>sign on hand</b>, <b>immovable before your eyes</b></li><li class=\"d0\">Later Judaism: literal <b>phylacteries</b> (scrolls on forehead, hand)</li><li class=\"d1\"><b>Christians</b> for centuries wore phylacteries with <b>NT verses</b> - not purely Jewish</li><li class=\"d1\">literal sense good <b>only with</b> the broader sense: in your <b>heart and mind</b>, not just stuck to the forehead</li><li class=\"d1\">physical things = <b>reminders</b> that help get it into heart/head</li><li class=\"d0\">Pastoral problem with <b>iconoclasm</b> (beyond theology)</li><li class=\"d1\">remove holy images → <b>whitewashed walls</b>; Protestant seminary profs worried even a <b>cross</b> might become an idol</li><li class=\"d1\">then what are people looking at all day? <b>computer, TV, phone, billboards</b></li><li class=\"d1\">preclude holy images → left with <b>profane images</b> at best, or <b>wickedness</b></li><li class=\"d1\">ancient Israel/Judaism <b>never iconoclastic</b>: synagogues with <b>imagery</b>, homes, phylacteries</li><li class=\"d0\">What should roll around in our heads</li><li class=\"d1\">not a <b>pop song</b> or <b>commercial jingle</b> - how about a <b>troparion</b>, a <b>hymn</b>? - \"a lot better\"</li><li class=\"d1\">everything stuck in our head <b>shapes</b> us</li></ul>"},{"t":2069.6,"lv":3,"h":"Teach children; family and community focus","b":"<ul><li class=\"d0\"><b>11:19-21</b> teach children: <b>sit, walk, lie down, rise up</b>; write on <b>doorposts and gates</b> → days \"<b>like days of heaven on earth</b>\"</li><li class=\"d1\">the <b>dinner table</b> is the place of conversation (\"I know\")</li><li class=\"d0\">Not individualistic language</li><li class=\"d1\">this is what <b>family and community life</b> focuses on</li><li class=\"d1\"><b>not</b> private religious beliefs \"we don't talk about in public\"</li></ul>"},{"t":2139.11,"lv":2,"h":"11:22-25 - Love, walk, hold fast","b":"<ul><li class=\"d0\"><b>11:22-25</b> love the Lord, <b>walk in all his ways</b>, <b>hold fast</b> to him</li><li class=\"d1\"><b>three things = summary of all the commandments</b></li><li class=\"d1\">last = <b>loyalty and allegiance</b></li><li class=\"d0\">Then he casts out nations → inherit <b>greater and mightier nations</b></li><li class=\"d1\">every place the sole of your foot treads: from desert and <b>anti-Lebanon</b> (\"instead of\" Lebanon, not against) to <b>Euphrates</b> to <b>western sea</b></li><li class=\"d1\"><b>no man can stand against you</b>; God puts <b>dread and fear</b> on the land</li><li class=\"d0\">You won't even have to <b>fight</b></li><li class=\"d1\">they're bigger, have <b>militaries, walled cities</b> - but they'll be <b>scared</b></li><li class=\"d1\">why? because of <b>Israel's God</b></li><li class=\"d1\">walk right in <b>as long as you remain faithful</b>; nothing to fear</li></ul>"},{"t":2248.07,"lv":2,"h":"11:26-28 - Blessing and curse; \"gods you have not known\"","b":"<ul><li class=\"d0\"><b>11:26-28</b> \"I set before you today a <b>blessing and a curse</b>\"</li><li class=\"d1\">blessing if obey; curse if go astray after <b>different gods you have not known</b></li><li class=\"d0\">\"Not known\" ≠ never heard the name</li><li class=\"d1\">they know <b>Baal</b> - remember <b>Baal Peor</b> in Numbers</li><li class=\"d1\">= <b>mutual knowing</b>: God knows Israel, Israel knows God; <b>relationship</b></li><li class=\"d1\">other gods are <b>strangers</b> - where were they when Israel was <b>enslaved in Egypt</b>, in the desert?</li><li class=\"d0\">Hebrew <b><i>yada</i></b> = to know - same word as <b>Gen 4</b>: \"Adam knew his wife\"</li><li class=\"d1\">not a euphemism, literal verb \"to know\"</li><li class=\"d1\">God compares his intimacy with Israel to <b>husband and wife</b></li></ul>"},{"t":2371.14,"lv":2,"h":"11:29-32 - Gerizim and Ebal","b":"<ul><li class=\"d0\"><b>11:29-30</b> put <b>blessing on Gerizim</b>, <b>curse on Ebal</b></li><li class=\"d1\">Levites pronounce blessings on Gerizim, curses on Ebal as they enter</li><li class=\"d1\">location: west, near <b>Gilgal</b>, beside the lofty <b>oak</b></li><li class=\"d0\">Israelites walk <b>between the two</b> → they must <b>choose which way</b>; an <b>enactment</b></li><li class=\"d0\">Q: like <b>doorposts</b>, or a <b>fork in the road</b>?</li><li class=\"d1\"><b>fork in the road</b> - valley between the mountains, left or right</li><li class=\"d0\">Q: is this why the <b>Samaritans</b> worshiped on <b>Mt Gerizim</b>?</li><li class=\"d1\">\"part of it\" - will get into it <b>in a few minutes</b>, next chapter</li><li class=\"d1\">chapter divisions <b>weren't original</b></li><li class=\"d0\"><b>11:31-32</b> cross Jordan, inherit, dwell; <b>be careful to do all the ordinances and judgments</b></li><li class=\"d1\">receiving the land but <b>called to choose</b> how to live and what consequence follows</li></ul>"},{"t":2491.25,"lv":3,"h":"Chapter break and the Samaritan Pentateuch","b":"<ul><li class=\"d0\">Good chapter break for content - but <b>not original</b></li><li class=\"d1\"><b>shift in topics</b></li><li class=\"d1\"><b>Samaritan Pentateuch</b> edit draws together things <b>not drawn together in the text</b></li></ul>"}]});
